@group
    @title=Gehtsoft Documentation Generator
    @key=main
    @ingroup=
    @brief=

    The Gehtsoft Documentation Generator is the tool to author and generate
    cross-language and cross-format documentation. It is main audience is
    for API developers, yet it can be used to create any documentation.

    The documentation source format is designed to allow:
    * Describe complex structured matters, including user documentation, programmatic API and data structures;
    * Provide rich text formatting abilities;
    * Keep all documentation source independent from final format (e.g. CHM, Web documentation, PDF);
    * Keep all documentation source is plain text files.

    DocGen is distributed under GPL license.

    The sources are available at github repository <https://github.com/gehtsoft-usa/docgen>

    An archive of precompiled binaries may be downloaded in the
    releases section of the repository.

    The nuget package is distributed via public Gehtsoft USA feed
    (see [link=tools]for details[/link]).

@end

@article
    @title=Tools
    @key=tools
    @ingroup=main
    @brief=The tools required to author the documentation

    To generate the documentation using Gehtsoft Documentation Generator
    you need to use [c]MSBuild[/c] or [c]dotnet build[/c] command. You need
    to have either Microsoft Visual Studio 15 or .NET Core 3.1 SDK (or above)
    installed. The tool supports both Windows and Linux build and
    is compatible with Ubuntu-based GIT actions.

    Please read [link=projectFile]Project File[/link] section for details
    on how MSBuild project file needs to be organized.

    You can use any text editor as an authoring tool, however we highly
    recommend to use Microsoft Visual Studio Code with the latest version
    of [eurl=https://www.myget.org/feed/gehtsoft-public/package/vsix/docgen]DocGen support extension[/eurl]
    Download the latest version of the extension and
    install it using the following command

    [c][b]code[/b] --install-extension docgen-[i]version[/i].vsix[/c]
@end